From: pdx203 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: bridge: metal2vulkan patch 0036, rotated copy back in 32 x 32 blocks

Carries bridge/patches/0036-rotated-copy-back-tiled.patch. TestUFO in landscape (sb1, rot-skip-back): skipping the copy backs took
backboardd swap submit->done from 20 to 4.8 ms and GPU per job from 4.5 to 1.2 ms, ~10 ms a copy back: bridge 0034's kernel
fetched one texel per invocation down a column of the frame image. Each workgroup now turns a 32 x 32 block through shared memory.

